From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: miogds <miogds@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:40:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shaders: xros_metal.py runs the chain's tools with a visionOS
 compile standard

A Metal library carries its platform, so the libraries the chain compiles
for the iPhone (ios_metal.py) are not visionOS libraries. The chain's
files are not changed for it: dm/ios/tools/xros_metal.py loads a second
copy of the module ios_metal with the target changed (the xros SDK,
-target air64-apple-xros26.0 in place of the iPhone's deployment target),
puts it where `import ios_metal` finds it, and runs a chain tool:

  IOSOUT=<visionOS folder> python3 dm/ios/tools/xros_metal.py dm/gfx/tools/dmsh_build.py ...
  python3 dm/ios/tools/xros_metal.py dm/gfx/tools/vk_shaders.py ... --ios <visionOS folder>

Every other flag is read from ios_metal.py as it is. The record names the
visionOS compile, so the reflection files say what was run and the
compiled-shader cache, keyed by the record, keeps the two platforms'
libraries apart. dmsh_build.py forks its workers, which therefore have
the copy too.

dm/ios/tests/test_xros_metal.py: only the target differs, the iPhone
module is untouched, a tool and its forked worker see the visionOS
standard, and the compiled library is tagged visionOS.

Not run on a game's shaders (none here), and scripts/build_ipa_from_nsp.py
does not call it yet: its shader steps still build iPhone libraries.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: visionOS is outside upstream's support matrix: the chain's tools compile visionOS shader libraries through a wrapper, the chain's files unchanged
Issue: none yet (miogds/NX2Apple, visionOS evaluation branch; to be filed before this goes to LNPANDY/NX2Apple)

---
 dm/ios/tests/test_xros_metal.py | 94 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dm/ios/tools/xros_metal.py      | 63 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 157 insertions(+)
